Z||000000||superman||01-21-2001||03:33 PM||||I own a 1984 2m4 and and it rains alot out here and the 13 inch wheels i got on there know handle like crap in the rain. I want to buy new rims and tires but I need to know if it would be better to have 15 or 16 inch wheels and what sze tires would you recomend.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Motorhead||01-22-2001||05:32 PM||||I'm running 195/70 14 on front with 235/60 14 in the rear on a set of tech rims right now.  Nothing can keep up with me on the off ramps.<BR>  I picked up a set of 15" GT rims real cheap and plan on running at least 235's on the rear with maybe 215's up front.  <BR>The low profile tires are really neat, but you reach a point where your wheel/tire combo looks like it came off a covered wagon.<BR>My 2 cents!<BR>Mike <P>------------------<BR>"The one who dies with the most toys wins!"<BR>  bluewater46@hotmail.com<BR>1986 coupe<BR>1984 coupe<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1372350&a=10234998&p=38686771&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||01-22-2001||07:15 PM||||17s! if your gunna spend the $ buy the wheels you like once not wheels you'll settle for twice... 18s are KILLER but tires are hard to get quickly. if your in some DEEP MTN. driving and waste a tire.. 17s are all over and NOT really pricey. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlow.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlow.jpg</A> <P>||||reg||1
